{% comment %}
  hz-foundation-spike — THROWAWAY Phase 0 proof harness for the horizon-blocks
  `group` layout engine + style helpers. NOT a real block; delete once Phase 1
  ships a real blocks/group.liquid wrapper + primitive blocks.

  It renders `snippets/group.liquid` with a hand-authored `children` blob of
  compact, differently-sized boxes + a short text-block + a divider (the real
  `text`/`divider` snippets are Phase 1, so we do NOT `{% render %}` them here),
  plus one genuinely-nested `{% render 'group' %}` driven by a section block, and
  exposes the group's core layout settings so the engine can be exercised from
  the theme editor.

  Hardening notes (Phase 0 closeout):
   - Children are compact boxes with EXPLICIT differing widths/heights so there is
     free space on both axes: alignment moves every child (row + column), and the
     group's `fit-content` width hugs the narrow content vs `fill` = 100%.
   - The group is wrapped in a fixed-height `__stage` (70vh) so `%` heights resolve
     (fill = 70vh, custom = X%, fit = auto) and row-mode has cross-axis room.
   - The nested `{% render 'group' %}` (a section block) makes an inner `.group-block`
     a direct flex child of the outer `.layout-panel-flex`, firing the
     `.layout-panel-flex--{row,column} > .group-block--{width,height}-*` flex rules.
     It defaults to fit/fit (compact, so it never steals the alignment free space);
     toggle its Width→Fill in a row parent or Height→Fill in a column parent to watch
     `flex: 1` grow it — mirroring real Phase-1 nested usage.

  Proves: the flex layout engine (direction / gap / alignment / width / height /
  padding), flex-child sizing of a nested group, the foundation var shim, and that
  every ported snippet renders without error. Does NOT prove preset typography —
  that is a Phase 1 type-preset system.
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'component-group.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%} Inner content for the genuinely-nested group (a real render 'group'). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture nested_children -%}
  <div class="spike-box spike-box--label" style="height: 3rem; padding-inline: 0.9rem;">NESTED</div>
  <div class="spike-box" style="width: 5rem; height: 3rem; background: rgba(160, 140, 200, 0.20);">5×3</div>
  <div class="spike-box" style="width: 7rem; height: 3rem; background: rgba(200, 150, 180, 0.20);">7×3</div>
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture children -%}
  <div class="spike-box" style="width: 6rem; height: 3rem; background: rgba(120, 160, 200, 0.18);">6×3</div>
  <div class="spike-box" style="width: 10rem; height: 5rem; background: rgba(200, 140, 120, 0.18);">10×5</div>
  <div class="spike-box" style="width: 8rem; height: 4rem; background: rgba(140, 190, 150, 0.18);">8×4</div>
  <div class="spike-box" style="width: 12rem; height: 6rem; background: rgba(200, 180, 120, 0.20);">12×6</div>

  <p class="text-block" style="margin: 0;">A short text-block child.</p>

  <div
    class="divider"
    style="align-self: stretch; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;"
  >
    <span
      class="divider__line"
      style="
        border-bottom: 2px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground, 18 18 18));
        flex-basis: 100%;
        min-height: 2px;
      "
    ></span>
  </div>

  <span class="spike-caption">↓ nested group (a real render 'group')</span>

  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- if block.type == 'nested_group' -%}
      {% render 'group',
        children: nested_children,
        settings: block.settings,
        shopify_attributes: block.shopify_attributes,
        background_color: block.settings.background_color,
        block_id: block.id
      %}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div class="hz-foundation-spike page-width">
  <p class="hz-foundation-spike__label">
    Horizon foundation spike (throwaway) — section&nbsp;{{ section.id }}
  </p>

  <div class="hz-foundation-spike__stage">
    {% render 'group',
      children: children,
      settings: section.settings,
      shopify_attributes: '',
      background_color: section.settings.background_color,
      block_id: section.id
    %}
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .hz-foundation-spike {
    padding-block: 5rem;
  }

  .hz-foundation-spike__label {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  /* Fixed-height stage so the group's `%` heights resolve and row mode has
     cross-axis room. Faint fill + outline so the stage bounds are legible. */
  .hz-foundation-spike__stage {
    position: relative;
    height: 70vh;
    background: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.03);
    outline: 1px solid rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.12);
  }

  /* Compact, labeled test boxes — explicit differing sizes leave free space on
     both axes so alignment repositions every child and fit-content stays narrow. */
  .hz-foundation-spike .spike-box {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border: 2px solid rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.4);
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.75);
    background: rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.04);
  }

  .hz-foundation-spike .spike-box--label {
    border-style: dashed;
    letter-spacing: 0.08rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .hz-foundation-spike .spike-caption {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03rem;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  /* Faint outline so every group-block's bounds are visible while testing
     width/height/padding — applies to the outer group AND the nested group. */
  .hz-foundation-spike .group-block {
    outline: 1px dashed rgba(var(--color-foreground), 0.35);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

